\subsection{Returns}{
(data.table | promise<data.table>) one row per symbol, with all
symbol fields returned by the API, converted to snake_case (empty when
Binance returns no symbols). Key columns include:
\itemize{
\item symbol (character) Trading pair identifier (e.g., \code{"BTCUSDT"}).
\item pair (character) Underlying pair.
\item contract_type (character) Contract type (e.g., \code{"PERPETUAL"}).
\item status (character) Trading status (\code{"TRADING"}, etc.).
\item base_asset (character) Base asset code (e.g., \code{"BTC"}).
\item quote_asset (character) Quote asset code (e.g., \code{"USDT"}).
\item margin_asset (character) Margin asset code (e.g., \code{"USDT"}).
\item price_precision (integer) Decimal precision for prices.
\item quantity_precision (integer) Decimal precision for quantities.
\item order_types (character) Semicolon-separated allowed order types.
Recover via \code{strsplit(dt$order_types[1], ";", fixed = TRUE)[[1]]}.
\item time_in_force (character) Semicolon-separated allowed
time-in-force values.
\item underlying_sub_type (character | NA) Semicolon-separated underlying
sub-types (\code{NA} when the symbol omits the field, as many
non-coin / index-style contracts do).
\item permission_sets (character | NA) Semicolon-separated permission sets
(\code{NA} when the symbol omits the field).
\item lot_min_qty (numeric | NA) Minimum order quantity (from LOT_SIZE
filter; \code{NA} when the symbol carries no LOT_SIZE filter).
\item lot_max_qty (numeric | NA) Maximum order quantity (from LOT_SIZE filter).
\item lot_step_size (numeric | NA) Quantity step size (from LOT_SIZE filter).
\item price_min (numeric) Minimum price (from PRICE_FILTER).
\item price_max (numeric) Maximum price (from PRICE_FILTER).
\item price_tick_size (numeric) Price tick size (from PRICE_FILTER).
\item min_notional (numeric | NA) Minimum notional value (from MIN_NOTIONAL
filter; \code{NA} when the symbol carries no MIN_NOTIONAL filter).
\item filters_raw (character) JSON-encoded copy of the full per-symbol
\code{filters} array. Preserves filter types not pulled into curated
columns (\code{PERCENT_PRICE}, \code{MARKET_LOT_SIZE}, \code{MAX_NUM_ORDERS},
\code{MAX_NUM_ALGO_ORDERS}, \code{MIN_NOTIONAL}'s extra fields, ...).
Recover with \code{jsonlite::fromJSON(dt$filters_raw[1])}. \code{NA} if
Binance returned no filters for the symbol.
}

Exchange-wide metadata returned by the same endpoint is exposed
via sibling methods: \code{get_rate_limits()}, \code{get_exchange_filters()},
\code{get_futures_assets()}. Server time is available via
\code{BinanceMarketData$get_server_time()}.
}
